    "first_comparison": "Reference versus delivery in paired blocks on the same installed DLL and same authored catalog; timeline arm isolates a demonstrated discrepancy.",
    "baseline": "Same safe stationary location and clear-bit stance, at least 500 ms measured stable riding, identical 600 ms preparation, neutral physical LS and triggers, D-pad plus single X. Do not compare held-A setup in the first experiment.",
    "rate": "Match the reference's 60 Hz simulation and normal time scale through existing local setting controls; measure tick/ms cadence and do not infer simulation rate from display refresh.",
    "evidence": "Join bounded playback and delivered-stick rows by seq; retain native FlipTrickType, timestamps, poll/tick/packet progression, gaps/drops, neutralization and reset. Cadence rows sample each active game tick and every changed output; cumulative poll counts expose additional same-tick reads without logging every identical poll. Reject incomplete timing evidence rather than promoting a partial trace.",
    "acceptance": "No promotion from local tests. Preserve all native misrecognitions. After selecting a proven change, at least 20 controlled trials per supported action with relevant context variation and no unexplained stuck states are required."
